comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-22T10:16:11.674Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: strict full all-status read of 3058 items completed with zero unreadable records and no omissions. Request-specific search and full live canonical history reads found completed adjacent work but no owner for this newly reported boundary. Reuse the existing capability lineage and retain prior closures."
  "2026-10-23T09:43:57.463Z","harness:codex","Active implementation paired with pm-gh1555: exact argv recovery for misplaced files/docs/test values, preserving refusal and no-mutation semantics. Apply pm-test-audit to regression authoring and verify complete current-head review before merge."
  "2026-10-23T09:51:27.265Z","harness:codex","Focused integration proves refused positional files/docs requests preserve item/history bytes, return exact normalized argv including quoted path bytes and presentation flags, and execute successfully only when that retry is explicitly invoked. Test metadata-only misuse requests the actual command without inventing executable argv. Five-file focused suite: 122 passed."
  "2026-10-23T10:15:42.371Z","harness:codex","Recovery hardening now serializes bare paths as quoted structured values, preserving literal commas and double quotes through --add parsing, with exact persisted-path assertions. SDK vocabulary gates metadata-only templates so an unknown key is not copied into an invalid retry. All changes stay in the existing two-item delivery."
  "2026-10-23T10:37:07.794Z","harness:codex","Final refusal metadata retains the actual item ID in command-missing templates and aligns linked_resource_positional_value catalog class/exit with CLI usage exit2. Generated catalog, public SDK snapshot, command fixture and refusal census are regenerated from owners. A catalog/CLI agreement regression is included."
  "2026-10-23T10:40:34.591Z","harness:codex","Architecture gate remediation: export resolveLinkedResourcePositionalRecovery and its typed receipt through the public SDK and host primitive facade; the CLI consumes that supported seam, and a public-root import drives its regression test. Do not extend private-import allowlists. Related request-admission normalization was moved out of the large execution module without increasing its file-length ceiling."
  "2026-10-23T11:22:33.862Z","harness:codex","Final linked run passed28 tests with recorded execution evidence, and public SDK import/typechecks pass. Code/static/conformance checks passed on the source revision; final graph/integrity checks were rerun after completing canonical metadata relationships and now pass. Package runtime acceptance through npx/bunx passes."
  "2026-10-23T11:29:43.209Z","harness:codex","Final scope check: metadata-only test templates retain the explicit tracker, item alias and presentation options without inventing an executable retry. The linked recovery suite passes 29 tests. A fresh packed artifact (SHA-256 522744a13dad96296b33c87c5ae7edd0b7a79f93190abd3197d8a67022fcf035) passes npm/npx and bun/bunx consumer checks for CLI/SDK assignment refusal without item/history writes, literal quoted/comma path recovery, and strict history verification. Type checking, generated-contract checks and changed-source lint pass."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T09:58:18.290Z","harness:codex","Recovery review: bare paths containing commas or quotes require structured-value quoting in addition to shell-safe argv rendering. A missing actual test command must remain a non-executable template, and unrelated/multiple mutations must never be silently combined."
  "2026-10-23T10:22:28.660Z","harness:codex","Latest-package changelog audit is available in2026.10.23. Final generation must follow item closure so reviewed Unreleased notes are based on the delivered fix, not merely registration or validation activity."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T10:01:23.893Z","harness:codex","A copyable recovery requires both shell-safe argv and the target option grammar. Quote literal path delimiters for structured --add parsing, and never supply an executable placeholder when the actual test command is missing."
